  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-rag",
      "text": "Local knowledge base RAG for DeepSeek Harness."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "Indexes project files (markdown, code, configs) and provides keyword search to find relevant context. No external APIs or embedding models needed -- pure local TF-IDF search."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile your-profile add dsh-plugin-rag\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "CLI",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "Search for relevant files",
      "text": "rag \"authentication\" ./src"
    },
    {
      "section": "Show index stats",
      "text": "rag --index ./src ./docs\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "What gets indexed",
      "text": "- Markdown (.md, .txt)\n- Code (.ts, .js, .py, .rs, .go, .java, .c, .cpp)\n- Config (.json, .yaml, .toml, .env)\n- Docs (.html, .xml, .sql, .graphql)\n\nSkips: node_modules, .git, dist, build, __pycache__"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "```yaml\n- id: rag\n  name: dsh-plugin-rag\n  config:\n    indexPaths: ['.']"
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "1. Scans directories for text files\n2. Builds a keyword index (TF-IDF scoring)\n3. Injects index stats into system prompt\n4. Agent uses CLI to search when needed\n\nNo embedding models, no external APIs, no heavy dependencies."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT -- YYTbit"
    }
  ],
